{
  "v": 1,
  "declinedShownMs": 6000,
  "about": "Tin Hat DM ringing (RINGING.md §5): what a dev.tinhat.call.decline {ring} room event means to this device. 'declined' = the room is a two-person room (dm), I am in (or joining) that room's call and the ring is one of MY call.member event ids: show the text and play the end tone; 'dismiss' = in a dm, MY other device declined the ring (one of the room's live call.member event ids from someone else) while my incoming card is up: the card and the ring go; 'none' = nothing. senderJoined = the decliner's room membership is join (someone who has left can't decline). rings: which call.member event ids own/live hold: the room's call.member state events that are live sessions (the shared live-session rule) of senders whose membership is exactly join, own = mine, live = others', in event order. A ring id is the core's call_decline_content rule: '$' + 1..254 more UTF-8 bytes, no control or white-space characters. Fresh = within 60 s of now either way. Byte-identical copies: web src/features/calls/testvectors/ringdecline.json (the owner), desktop crates/app/src/testvectors/ringdecline.json. Each case: event, ctx {me, dm, senderJoined, inCallHere, cardUp, ownRings, liveRings} at now, want. texts: [display name, the words shown]. declinedShownMs: how long the caller's '<name> declined' stays on screen (web toast, desktop passive notification); gates read the stable log line / DOM marker instead (tools README).",
